WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.150
The K D S root key deserves its own slide.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:08.872
In any forest, you create it with Add K
D S Root Key, dash Effective Immediately,

3
00:00:08.872 --> 00:00:13.362
and then you wait, up to ten hours,
before a G M S A can be created.

4
00:00:13.362 --> 00:00:16.298
Learn's K D S page offers
a key backdated ten hours,

5
00:00:16.298 --> 00:00:19.893
but only for a test environment
with one domain controller,

6
00:00:19.893 --> 00:00:23.488
and Learn's containers page says
not to use it in production.

7
00:00:23.488 --> 00:00:25.300
So: never in production.

8
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.775
And create only one.

9
00:00:26.775 --> 00:00:32.090
Learn says more than one key makes G M S As
start failing after a password rotation,

10
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:35.184
and a deleted and re-created
key can stay cached,

11
00:00:35.184 --> 00:00:38.930
so the K D C has to be restarted
on every domain controller.
